<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tadun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 207</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tadun (died 207) was a chieftain of the Wuhuan, a nomadic people of the north-eastern Chinese frontier, who led the Wuhuan of Liaoxi at the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Eastern Han</a>. He allied with the warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shao">Yuan Shao</a> and later sheltered Yuan Shao's sons Yuan Shang and Yuan Xi. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a>'s army defeated and killed him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-white-wolf-mountain">Battle of White Wolf Mountain</a> in 207, ending Wuhuan independence.</p></div>
